# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# t4port — git hygiene
#
# Two hard rules:
#   1. never commit Activision/game data (.ff, .iwd, .iwi, .gsc, CoDWaW*.exe,
#      the sample textures in re/samples/) — the engine reads it from a local
#      copy of the game, it is not redistributable;
#   2. never commit build caches / toolchains / extracted sysroots.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- game data (Activision) — NEVER publish ------------------------------
*.ff
*.iwd
*.iwi
*.gsc
*.csc
*.bik
CoDWaW*.exe
plutonium*.exe
re/samples/

# --- build outputs (rebuildable; per-OS binaries in dist/ are committed) --
build/
**/obj/
*.o
*.obj
source_original/build/

# --- toolchains, sysroots, package caches ---------------------------------
tools/.zig/
freebsd/.sysroot/
windows/.sysroot/
.zlib/
.zlib-freebsd/
base.txz
*.tar.xz
*.tar.gz
.flatpak/
.flatpak-builder/
*.flatpak

# --- editors / OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- python bytecode caches ------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- dev tree (port_test/): build variants + flatpak caches ---------------
build-asan/
build-freebsd/
.flatpak-build/
.flatpak-repo/
a.out

# game-derived samples em qualquer subarvore
**/re/samples/
